        en: { name: 'Noetzie Beach and its castles', description: 'A secluded cove at the mouth of the Noetzie River, overlooked by several private turreted stone “castles” built as holiday homes. Sand, forested slopes and hardly anyone around.', tip: 'From Knysna, drive east on the N2 and turn onto the gravel Noetzie Road; from the upper car park a steep ten-minute path leads down to the beach.' },
